Completed the **38-page original-record review**, including dated chronologies, source/custody tables, claim assessments, contrary evidence, prioritized missing records, and proposed repository updates:

[:chatgpt-content-reference{index="4"}](https://chatgpt.com/library?file_id=libfile_2dc51d60b40081919217c71b85c41623&account_id=personal)

**The most consequential findings:**

- **Options:** The SEC records **117,000 UAL shares short alongside 115,000 AMR shares long**. The AMR purchase alone therefore cannot establish an overall portfolio loss. Later Commission memoranda correct widely repeated trading counts. The separate **$85,000 loss finding concerns another fund**. Statistical anomalies remain relevant, but neither their percentiles nor the public investigative summaries independently establish ownership, complete exposure, or foreknowledge. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="0"}
- **Insurance:** The 2013 findings distinguish **$4.582 billion paid across the main-site claims** from **$4.091 billion allocated to WTCP**. Neither is personal profit. The report preserves differing published totals, missing payment schedules, unresolved owner distributions, and the subsequent appeal’s qualifications. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="1"}
- **KBR and Carlyle:** GAO records **$56.515 million in RIO award fees paid**, distinct from contract ceilings and net income. United Defense’s **$289.7 million August 2001 dividend preceded the attacks**; later shareholder proceeds and fees require separate accounting and ultimate-beneficiary tracing. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="2"}

No authenticated preattack connection to attack arrangements emerged from the acquired records. That bounded finding **does not require direct UMS–hijacker contact** or dispose of every compartmented hypothesis.

The three exact Mac-path reports remained unavailable; continuity came from the public integration and two recovered prior reviews. The report identifies that limitation explicitly. **All repository updates remain proposals; the repository was not edited.**

